<h2>Wabash Valley weather</h2>
<p>Terre Haute sits on the Wabash River near the state’s western border, directly in the path of storms crossing from the west. Hail, damaging winds and tornadoes are part of most springs. Sullivan County, just to the south, was struck by a destructive tornado on March 31, 2023, a reminder of how quickly storms in the valley can turn severe. Winter ice storms and river flooding along the Wabash add to the mix.</p>
<h2>Housing in Terre Haute</h2>
<p>Farrington’s Grove is one of the state’s largest historic districts, filled with Victorian, Queen Anne and Craftsman homes with wood siding, complex rooflines and ornate trim. Collett Park and the Twelve Points area have early-20th-century homes, while neighborhoods near Indiana State University and Rose-Hulman include many rentals. Post-war ranches fill much of the south and east sides.</p>
<h2>Disputes we see in Terre Haute</h2>
<ul>
<li>Historic wood siding and trim replaced with vinyl in the carrier’s estimate.</li>
<li>Complex Victorian rooflines measured without accounting for turrets, dormers and steep pitch.</li>
<li>Rental properties where code upgrades are required during repair.</li>
<li>Interior water losses in older homes with original plumbing.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Communities we cover</h2>
<p>Terre Haute, West Terre Haute, Seelyville, Riley, Brazil, Sullivan, Clinton and the surrounding Wabash Valley.</p>

